  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collective Initiative: Shifting Power for Resilience and Value of Local Actors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The joint Action Against Hunger, ActionAid and Age International (through their implementing partner HelpAge) Collective Initiative project seeks to address these root causes that create obstacles for local civil society actors to grow organically through an integrated, multi-layered capacity strengthening approach that goes beyond the buzzword of &#x2018;participation&#x2019; and conceptualises capacity strengthening as inherently partner-developed, partner-driven, and partner-led. The three members of the consortium come from different backgrounds and combine vast experience in multisectoral humanitarian action (Action Against Hunger), nexus-focused rights-based work (ActionAid) and a strong focus on older people (Age International) but have all worked on strengthening local partnerships through different approaches. The project&#x2019;s overall objective is to showcase pathways to the DEC community that have the potential to strengthen the voice and agency of local actors through a shifting-the-power approach. This will be achieved by giving local actors the means to develop their own capacity with tailored support from their international counterparts, while creating sharing space that allow for participation of rights holders, communities and local authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
